 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, four failing tests are not directly the `partitioned` TypeError. The subagent's list of ~20 cause-related tests plus these four accounts for the 24 failures only approximately; its exact counts were not fully reconciled.\n\n1. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra`. The async dependency isn't installed in this environment. This is an environment issue, unrelated to Werkzeug.\n\n2. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `request.max_form_memory_size` is `None` instead of 500000. This is likely a feature missing from Werkzeug 3.0.3, so it probably shares the Werkzeug-version cause but is a different missing API.\n\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: a pytest-related error that the subagent did not diagnose, so its cause is unknown.\n\n4. **`test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name`**: returns an HTML error page instead of `b'value set'`. This is probably the same `set_cookie` failure surfacing as a 500, but the subagent didn't confirm it, so it may belong with the main cause.\n\nOnly #1 is clearly independent. #2 and #4 are probably related to the Werkzeug version, and #3 needs further investigation.",
